<!-- INFORMATION WE COLLECT — VISITORS -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-visitors">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Information We Collect from Visitors</h2>
        <p>
            If you read this website without filling out a form or otherwise identifying
            yourself, we do not collect personal information about you. Anonymous visits
            produce only privacy-preserving page-view counts, which tell us which pages
            people read, and the standard request logs every web host keeps.
        </p>
        <p>
            Specifically, anonymous visits generate the following information, collected
            by our hosting provider, Vercel:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Page views</strong> &mdash; which pages were visited, at what
                approximate time, and in what order.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Referrer</strong> &mdash; the website (if any) that sent you to
                ours.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Approximate country</strong> &mdash; determined from the general
                geographic region of your internet connection. We do not collect city-
                level or precise geolocation data.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Device type and operating system</strong> &mdash; for example,
                &ldquo;mobile iOS&rdquo; or &ldquo;desktop Windows.&rdquo;
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>IP address</strong> &mdash; retained temporarily in server request
                logs by our hosting providers for operational and security purposes, not
                used to profile you.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            This analytics data is anonymized. It is not tied to your name or any other
            identifier, and we make no attempt to reconstruct your identity from it. It
            never includes anything you write on this site, and the page addresses it
            records leave out everything after a question mark.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

