<section class="content-section" id="privacy-members">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Your reflections stay on your device</h2>
        <p>
            When you write an answer to a reflection question on this site, your words are
            kept only in this browser, on this device. They are never sent to us. We cannot
            read them, recover them or hand them to anyone, because we never have them.
        </p>
        <p>
            To keep your reflections, download them from the Reflections panel or from
            <a href="/my-reflections/" class="text-gold">My Discipleship Journal</a>, as a Word
            document, a PDF or a text file. If you clear your browser’s data, use a
            different browser or change devices, anything you have not downloaded will be
            gone. If you share this computer with others, use “Clear my answers from this
            browser” when you are finished.
        </p>
        <p>
            <em>Keep My Commandments</em> (commandments.brotheraaron.org) is a separate app
            with its own optional account. What you save there is stored on its server and
            is governed by that app.
        </p>
        <p>
            Accounts created while this site was being tested remain on our server until
            they are deleted. Nothing new is added to them.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- INFORMATION WE COLLECT — FORMS -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-forms">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Information We Collect from Forms</h2>
        <p>
            One form on this site accepts information:
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>The newsletter signup form</strong>, which appears in the site footer
            and on the Connect page, collects your name and email address. We also record
            the time of your submission and your IP address for the limited purpose of
            preventing spam and abuse of the form.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Messages you send by email.</strong> The Connect page invites you to
            write to Brother Aaron at host@brotheraaron.org. Your message, your email
            address and anything else you include reach his inbox and nowhere else; the
            site itself receives nothing.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION -->
<section class="content-section" id="privacy-use">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>
            We use the information described above only for the following purposes:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>To operate the website.</strong> Analytics help us understand which
                chapters and pages are reaching people, so we can improve them and
                prioritize what to write next.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>To send you the newsletter</strong> if you have subscribed to it,
                and to honor your choice if you later unsubscribe.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>To respond to messages</strong> you send Brother Aaron by email.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>To protect the integrity of the site</strong> &mdash; preventing
                abuse, detecting attempts to compromise the system, and honoring mandatory
                reporting obligations described in our
                <a href="/community-guidelines/" class="text-gold">Fellowship Agreement</a>
                and <a href="/safety/" class="text-gold">Safety &amp; Support</a> pages.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We do <strong>not</strong> use your information for advertising, profile-
            building, resale, or any purpose unrelated to the ministry. We do not combine
            your information with data from third parties to build a richer picture of
            you.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- STORAGE AND SECURITY -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-security">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>How We Store and Secure Your Information</h2>
        <p>
            Submissions from the newsletter form pass through a
            small application server operated by the ministry and hosted on a private,
            password-protected server at PythonAnywhere. Connections to our servers are
            encrypted in transit using HTTPS. Your reflections are not stored there; they
            never leave your device.
        </p>
        <p>
            We take reasonable measures to protect your information, including keeping
            our software up to date, limiting administrative access, and periodically
            reviewing our security posture. However, no system connected to the internet
            can be guaranteed to be perfectly secure. If a security incident affects your
            data in a way that is likely to cause you harm, we will notify you as promptly
            as we are able.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- THIRD-PARTY SERVICES -->
<section class="content-section" id="privacy-third-parties">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
            Running a website requires the help of a small number of outside service
            providers. We have chosen providers that respect user privacy and minimize
            data collection. Each one is listed below, along with what information it
            receives and why.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; provides our domain-name system and the
            media server at <em>media.wordsofplainness.org</em>, which delivers the
            site&rsquo;s audio and banner images. Cloudflare receives your IP address and
            the standard information sent by your browser only when your browser loads a
            file from that media server. Cloudflare runs no analytics on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Vercel</strong> &mdash; hosts the website itself and provides our web
            analytics. Vercel Web Analytics runs from this site&rsquo;s own address, uses
            no cookies, and identifies visitors only by a temporary, anonymous code that
            resets every twenty-four hours, so no one can be followed from one day to the
            next or from one site to another. Vercel receives request logs as part of
            hosting the site.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>PythonAnywhere</strong> &mdash; hosts the application server that
            receives submissions from the newsletter form.
            PythonAnywhere sees this information only because it operates the
            infrastructure on which the server runs.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Buttondown</strong> &mdash; delivers our newsletter. If you have
            subscribed, Buttondown stores your email address, name, and subscription
            preferences in order to send you the newsletter and honor your unsubscribe
            requests.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Google Fonts</strong> &mdash; provides the typefaces used throughout
            the site. When your browser loads a page, it requests these typefaces from
            Google, and Google can therefore observe the request (including your IP
            address) as part of serving the font file.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Discord</strong> &mdash; provides our community discussion platform.
            Discord is not integrated into the website in a way that transfers data
            about you; it is linked as an external destination. If you choose to join
            our Discord server, your interaction with Discord is governed by
            Discord&rsquo;s own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>churchofjesuschrist.org</strong> &mdash; the external destination for
            every scripture citation on this site. We do not send data to the Church
            website; if you follow a scripture link, your browser transmits the usual
            request information directly to their servers.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- COOKIES AND LOCAL STORAGE -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-cookies">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
            This website does not use tracking cookies. It does not participate in any
            advertising network. It does not employ third-party analytics that track
            users across multiple sites. Under the rules that govern cookie consent in
            most jurisdictions, strictly necessary storage does not require a consent
            banner, which is why you do not see one on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
            The site does use your browser&rsquo;s <em>local storage</em> for a small
            number of functional purposes:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Reader preferences</strong> &mdash; your chosen font size and
                similar display settings.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Reading progress, narration position and bookmarks</strong> &mdash;
                so the site can remember where you left off.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Anthem player state</strong> &mdash; whether the ministry anthem
                audio controls are expanded or collapsed.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Your reflections</strong> &mdash; your answers, journal entries and
                questions, kept only on this device until you clear them. See
                <a href="#privacy-members" class="text-gold">Your reflections stay on your device</a>, above.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            All of this local storage lives on your own device and is never transmitted
            to us or to any third party. You can clear it at any time through your browser&rsquo;s
            settings.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CHILDREN'S PRIVACY -->
<section class="content-section" id="privacy-children">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            This ministry is written for adults and is not directed to children under
            the age of thirteen. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
            children under thirteen. If we learn that we have inadvertently collected
            such information, we will delete it promptly. If you are a parent or
            guardian and you believe your child has provided personal information to
            this site, please contact us at the address below and we will assist you.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- YOUR RIGHTS -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-rights">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Your Rights Over Your Information</h2>
        <p>
            The information on this site belongs to the people it describes. Whether or
            not the law where you live uses these words, we will honor the following
            rights for everyone:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to know</strong> what information we have about you.
                You can ask us and we will tell you.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to correct</strong> information about you that is
                inaccurate. Write to us and we will correct it.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to delete</strong> the information we hold about you.
                Write to us and we will remove it from our active systems within thirty
                days of your request, subject to any narrow exceptions described in
                <a href="#privacy-retention" class="text-gold">Data Retention</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to export</strong> your reflections, journal entries,
                witness testimonies, and commitments. They are kept on your own device,
                and you can download them at any time from the Reflections panel or from
                <a href="/my-reflections/" class="text-gold">My Discipleship Journal</a>. You do not
                need to ask our permission.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to withdraw consent</strong> to any communication you
                previously agreed to. Every newsletter email contains a one-click
                unsubscribe link. You can also write to us and we will remove you.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The right to be told about meaningful changes</strong> to how
                we handle your information.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, write to us at the address in the
            <a href="#privacy-contact" class="text-gold">Contact</a> section below. We
            do not require you to cite a statute or prove a jurisdiction; asking is
            enough.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- DATA RETENTION -->
<section class="content-section" id="privacy-retention">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
            We retain different kinds of information for different lengths of time:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Deleted information</strong> &mdash; when we delete information at
                your request, it is removed from active systems within thirty days. A small
                amount may persist briefly in encrypted backups that are themselves rotated
                on a normal retention schedule.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Newsletter unsubscribes</strong> &mdash; when you unsubscribe,
                your email address is retained in a suppression list solely so that we
                do not accidentally re-add you in the future. It is never used for any
                other purpose.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Email you send to Brother Aaron</strong> is kept in his inbox as
                part of normal correspondence until he deletes it. It is not systematically
                purged. You may ask him to delete any message you have sent, and he will.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Anonymous analytics data</strong> is kept by Vercel for the limited
                period our hosting plan provides and is then discarded. The anonymous daily
                visitor code is reset every twenty-four hours.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Server request logs</strong> are retained by our hosting
                providers on their standard rolling schedules and are used for
                operational and security purposes only.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Aggregated, anonymized engagement statistics</strong> gathered
                before November 2026 may be retained indefinitely. The site no longer
                collects them. They contain no information that identifies any individual.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CHANGES -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-changes">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time as the ministry grows, as the
            services we rely on change their own practices, or as the laws governing
            online privacy evolve. Every version of this policy is dated at the bottom
            of the page. Material changes will be announced in the newsletter and in a
            short notice on the site.
        </p>
        <p>
            Continued use of the website after a revision constitutes acceptance of the
            revised policy. If you do not accept a revision, you may stop using the site
            at any time.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CONTACT -->
<section class="content-section" id="privacy-contact">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Contact About Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            Questions about this policy, requests to exercise the rights described above,
            and any other privacy-related correspondence should be sent to Brother Aaron
            by email at <a href="mailto:host@brotheraaron.org?subject=Privacy" class="text-gold">host@brotheraaron.org</a>,
            with the subject &ldquo;Privacy.&rdquo; We respond personally; there is no automated privacy
            queue and no call center. Your question reaches a person.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- A WORD FROM BROTHER AARON -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="privacy-brother-aaron">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>A Word from Brother Aaron</h2>
        <p>
            A privacy policy is a legal document, but for a ministry it is also a
            promise. What you write in your journal belongs to you. What you confess in
            your reflection is between you and the Lord. What you offer as witness
            belongs to you until you choose to share it. I do not read private entries.
            No one on the ministry staff reads private entries. They never leave your
            device. They stay where you wrote them, for you alone, until you choose to
            keep them, share them or clear them away.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you choose to share what you have written—with your family, with your
            religious leaders, or with the people who matter most to you—that choice is
            yours, made in your own way and your own time. If you choose to share it with
            me, write to me, and I will receive it with care.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you trust this ministry with words you have never said to anyone else, I
            want you to know that trust is received with the gravity it deserves. That is
            not a promise I can prove in a document. It is a promise I can only keep by
            the way this ministry is operated over time. I will keep it.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.65;">
            Words of Plainness Privacy Policy v{{ privacyPolicy.version }} &mdash; Aaron Powner Publishing &mdash;
            {{ privacyPolicy.date }}. This policy is reviewed periodically and updated as the
            ministry&rsquo;s scope and the services we rely on change.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
